sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant POS as POS Client
    participant GQL as Apollo Gateway
    participant ID as Identity Service
    participant CART as Cart Service
    participant CACHE as Inventory Cache (Redis)
    participant SAP as SAP ECC

    Note over POS,SAP: Operation: Store Associate looks up a customer's online cart by scanning the loyalty QR code

    POS->>GQL: GraphQL cartLookupByLoyaltyQr(qrToken) [p95 35ms]
    GQL->>ID: Resolve loyalty QR to customer identity [p95 25ms]
    ID-->>GQL: customerId + auth context [p95 10ms]
    GQL->>CART: Get active online cart for customerId [p95 20ms]
    CART-->>GQL: cart with 4 line items [p95 15ms]

    loop Per line item availability check
        GQL->>CACHE: Check store availability by SKU/store [p95 5ms]
        CACHE-->>GQL: availability result [p95 3ms]
    end

    alt Inventory cache miss on one SKU
        GQL->>SAP: Inline stock lookup for missing SKU [p95 400ms]
        SAP-->>GQL: stock result [p95 120ms]
        Note over GQL,SAP: Slow fallback path; use only on cache miss
    else Cache hit for all SKUs
        Note over GQL,CACHE: Fast path stays off SAP runtime dependency
    end

    GQL-->>POS: Cart + availability statuses for store [p95 25ms]

    Note over POS,SAP: Happy-path estimate ≈ 162ms p95 before POS render
    Note over POS,SAP: Cache-miss path adds ~520ms p95 → ≈ 682ms p95 before POS render
    Note over POS,SAP: Bottleneck: SAP ECC inline lookup at ~400ms p95 dominates when the inventory cache misses. Primary mitigation lever: cache warm-up on Kafka stock events; secondary: degrade to "stock unknown — confirm with floor staff" on cache miss.
